WEBVTT - AeroSense AI Demonstration Subtitles (v2)

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.799
Air pollution is one of the most critical public health emergencies of our time.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.800
Across South Asia and the Indo-Gangetic Plain, hundreds of millions wake up under thick winter smog.

3
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:24.800
Yet a single colored AQI number doesn't tell a mother when to open windows, or an asthmatic grandfather his inhaled particulate mass.

4
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:34.799
Welcome to AeroSense AI — the Clean-Air Decision Engine, built for PromptWars Challenge 6.

5
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:43.189
Our mission: Know the air. Predict the risk. Protect your family. Prove the impact.

6
00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:52.189
To see how AeroSense AI works in practice, let's follow an illustrative family scenario — the Sharma family in Bengaluru.

7
00:00:52.390 --> 00:01:03.189
The parents commute along Outer Ring Road, 8-year-old Aarav has soccer practice, and Grandfather plans his daily walk.

8
00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:14.189
Is outdoor air safe for soccer? Which pollutant is peaking? Is pollution trapping closer to the ground?

9
00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:27.250
Traditional apps only give a number. AeroSense AI guides their decisions from sunrise to bedtime.

10
00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:35.250
Here is AeroSense AI, live on the web at aero-sense-ai-psi.vercel.app.

11
00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:44.250
Deep ink slate accented by emerald and teal, built for high contrast and accessibility.

12
00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:54.250
Our deterministic physical engines do all the science. Generative AI only plans and explains.

13
00:01:54.450 --> 00:02:03.250
Every metric comes from validated physics and official standards, with zero hallucinated numbers.

14
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:12.660
Live snapshot bar and introductions to our Five Pillars: Know, Predict, Protect, Home, and Act.

15
00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:17.660
We are now inside the Overview Dashboard.

16
00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:27.660
In Bengaluru, our engine calculates the Indian National AQI at 139, in the 'Moderate' category.

17
00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:37.660
Ozone is the dominant pollutant at 127 µg/m³, while PM2.5 is measured at 24.2 µg/m³.

18
00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:49.660
Under CPCB standards, this falls in the 'Good' sub-index band, though slightly above the WHO 24h guideline of 15 µg/m³.

19
00:02:49.860 --> 00:03:07.840
3D Atmospheric Inversion Scene: 1,045m boundary layer, winds at 11.8 km/h, Inversion Risk score just 24/100.

20
00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:17.840
Pillar 1: Live Air Intelligence. Inspect PM2.5, PM10, NO2, SO2, CO, and Ozone.

21
00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:27.840
Every sub-index is computed strictly according to CPCB October 2014 breakpoint rules.

22
00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:38.840
Switching from Bengaluru to Delhi-NCR in the location selector updates the entire dashboard.

23
00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:57.330
In Delhi, AQI surges to 255 (Poor) dominated by PM2.5 at 106.9 µg/m³ — over 4x higher than Bengaluru.

24
00:03:57.530 --> 00:04:02.330
Pillar 2: Pollution Forecast and Atmospheric Risk.

25
00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:12.330
During cold winter evenings, ground cooling creates thermal inversions, trapping surface air.

26
00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:25.330
AeroSense AI plots a forward 48-hour hourly outlook analyzing surface, 925 hPa, and 850 hPa lapse rates.

27
00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:44.630
Backtest Calibration Panel transparently reports MAE, RMSE, and bias against historical station readings.

28
00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:55.630
Pillar 3: Family Protection. All profiles stored strictly on-device in browser IndexedDB.

29
00:04:55.830 --> 00:05:06.630
Personal identifiers stripped before any external call, passing only anonymized age groups to Gemini.

30
00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:18.630
AeroSense AI applies the US EPA formula: Inhaled dose equals concentration times ventilation rate times duration.

31
00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:30.630
Aarav's soccer dose is 13.3 µg, compared against a daily child reference budget of 120 µg based on WHO guidelines.

32
00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:42.250
Grandfather's respiratory risk labeled with explicit Berkeley Earth non-clinical comparative disclaimers.

33
00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:51.250
Pillar 4: Indoor Air Advisor, addressing the 90% of life spent indoors.

34
00:05:51.450 --> 00:06:01.250
AeroSense AI uses a first-principles PM2.5 Mass-Balance Differential Equation.

35
00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:11.250
In Bengaluru (PM2.5 24.2 µg/m³), the engine recommends 'Open Windows for Natural Ventilation'.

36
00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:20.250
In Delhi (PM2.5 106.9 µg/m³), the equation reverses to 'Seal Windows and Run Purifier'.

37
00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:28.550
Purifier CADR sizing calculator and blueprints for a DIY Corsi-Rosenthal Box.

38
00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:37.550
Pillar 5: Act — The What-If Simulator. Proving the measurable impact of sustainable choices.

39
00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:49.550
Priya's 15km commute shift from scooter to Namma Metro reduces in-cabin particulate penetration by 85%.

40
00:06:49.750 --> 00:07:00.550
Avoids over 5 µg of inhaled particulate mass and 495 grams of vehicular CO2 tailpipe emissions per trip.

41
00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:13.450
Clicking View Impact Receipt generates an auditable receipt with baseline, delta, and engine version impact@1.0.0.

42
00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:21.450
AeroSense Drone Lab for low-altitude vertical atmospheric profiling.

43
00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:33.450
Radical engineering honesty: status displays 'Not Connected' while prototype is in the workshop.

44
00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:42.450
Clicking Launch Flight Demonstration illuminates an explicit amber 'SIMULATED' badge.

45
00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:54.490
Telemetry HUD animates quadcopter ascent up to 120m, mapping vertical boundary layer traps.

46
00:07:54.690 --> 00:08:02.490
Community Hub: Individual household actions scale to neighborhood impact.

47
00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:12.490
Clean-Air Decision Score (0-100) measures verified household mitigation actions only.

48
00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:24.010
Specialized Sectoral Action Plans for schools, eldercare homes, and construction sites.

49
00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:34.009
AeroSense AI Copilot powered by Google Gemini 2.5 Flash with strict deterministic facts.

50
00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:44.009
Input sanitized against prompt injection and demographic data stripped.

51
00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:57.009
Asking for Bengaluru precautions, Gemini cites Fact #1: AQI 139 and Fact #3: PM2.5 24.2.

52
00:08:57.210 --> 00:09:09.009
Recommends midday ventilation, metro transit, and identifies clean air window from noon to 3 PM.

53
00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:21.110
Server-side validator audits every number against facts registry, rejecting unsupported claims.

54
00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:31.110
Clean-Air Daily Planner synthesizes intelligence into a 24-hour visual routine for Sharma family.

55
00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:52.960
7 AM ventilation, 8:30 AM metro transit, 1-4 PM outdoor window, and 7 PM evening seal advisory.

56
00:09:53.160 --> 00:10:02.960
Spatial Air and Incident Map at /map. Concentric radar rings at 10, 25, and 50 kilometers.

57
00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:14.960
Wind moving at 11.8 km/h towards 226° SW; downwind plume sector labeled as mathematical estimate.

58
00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:32.100
Transparent engineering honesty: unconfigured or clear upstream feeds display verified targets without fake fires.

59
00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:40.100
Under the hood: Decoupled 5-layer architecture powering AeroSense AI.

60
00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:53.100
Layer 1: Ingestion. Layer 2: Fusion, privacy, prompt safety. Layer 3: Eight offline TypeScript engines.

61
00:10:53.300 --> 00:11:07.100
Layer 4: Fact Registry and Impact Receipts. Layer 5: Next.js 15, Three.js 3D, and 11 Indian languages with Urdu RTL.

62
00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:18.100
120 passing Vitest tests. Developed by Somashekhar Vani for PromptWars Challenge 6.

63
00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:31.210
AeroSense AI: Know the air. Predict the risk. Protect your family. Prove the impact.

